meta {
  name: Members - Search
  type: http
  seq: 49
}

get {
  url: {{BASE_URL}}/api/v1/communities/nswswk8w8wso0ko8owwk8k0w/members?query=ada&limit=8
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

docs {
  Members of the community whose username, or a word of their name, starts with the query (mention autocomplete). Same fields and the same people as Members - List (cuid, name, username, avatar_url, headline, role, member_since, tags, in_member_list): a member who hides from the member list is not found, also by the exact username, except by the managers and by the member themself (#1466). The headline (#1688) is empty unless the member shows it, and the search does not read it. The server trims the query and keeps its first 100 characters. Without a sort parameter, the usernames that start with the query come first; with sort=name or sort=newest, the sort alone gives the order (see Members - List). Members of the community only.
}
